<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<catalogue xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/catalogueSchema" id="cust-36-0000000" name="Custodian Brothers (v3.6.0 roster baseline)" revision="1" battleScribeVersion="2.03" library="false" gameSystemId="b174-c09d-3660-f001" gameSystemRevision="3"><sharedRules><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c100" name="Battleborn" hidden="false"><description>If a unit where most models have this rule is Shaken at the beginning of the round, roll one die. On a 4+, it stops being Shaken.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c101" name="Fearless" hidden="false"><description>When a unit where most models have this rule fails a Morale test, roll one die. On a 4+, the test counts as passed.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c102" name="Hero" hidden="false"><description>A Hero with Tough(6) or less may join a multi-model unit that does not already include another Hero; it may take Morale tests for the unit, and is generally allocated wounds after ordinary models.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c103" name="Tough(X)" hidden="false"><description>This model must suffer X wounds before being removed. Allocate and track wounds on each Tough model rather than removing it after a single wound.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c104" name="Versatile Expert" hidden="false"><description>When this unit is activated, choose one effect until the end of that activation: models with this rule in this unit gain AP(+1) when attacking, or gain +1 to hit rolls when attacking.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c105" name="Strider" hidden="false"><description>Ignores the effects of difficult terrain when moving.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c106" name="Armor(2+)" hidden="false"><description>This unit has Armor (2+), giving it a 2+ armour protection rating when defending against attacks.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c107" name="Scout" hidden="false"><description>After other units have deployed, this model may make a special pre-game move of up to 12", ignoring terrain. If both players have Scouts, roll off and alternate placing or moving them.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c108" name="Stealth" hidden="false"><description>Enemies suffer -1 to hit when shooting at a unit where all models have Stealth from more than 12" away.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c109" name="Relentless" hidden="false"><description>When using a Hold action and shooting, unmodified rolls of 6 to hit count as two hits. Only the original hit counts as an unmodified 6 for other rules.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c10a" name="Fast" hidden="false"><description>Moves farther than standard units: +2" on Advance and +4" on Rush and Charge.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c10b" name="Ambush" hidden="false"><description>This unit may be kept off the table at deployment. At the start of a round after the first, deploy it anywhere more than 9" from enemy units, following the Ambush deployment order.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c10c" name="Immobile" hidden="false"><description>This unit may only use Hold actions.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c10d" name="Transport(X)" hidden="false"><description>This model transports up to X eligible models. Passengers may deploy inside, embark by moving into contact, or disembark during a move and be placed within 6". If the transport is destroyed, passengers take dangerous terrain tests and become Shaken.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c10e" name="Fear(X)" hidden="false"><description>When deciding who won a melee, add X to the number of wounds dealt by this unit.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c10f" name="Vanguard" hidden="false"><description>After deployment, this model may be placed anywhere fully within 9" of its original position, more than 9" away from enemy units without Vanguard.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c110" name="Artillery" hidden="false"><description>This unit is classed as Artillery and is subject to the artillery movement and firing restrictions.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c111" name="Cumbersome" hidden="false"><description>May only use Hold or Advance actions, and cannot shoot when moving.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c112" name="Aircraft" hidden="false"><description>This model is an Aircraft, which uses aircraft-specific movement and targeting rules.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c113" name="AP(X)" hidden="false"><description>When blocking hits from this weapon, the target gets -X to its Defense rolls.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c114" name="Blast(X)" hidden="false"><description>This weapon ignores cover. After resolving its other special rules, each hit is multiplied by X, to a maximum number of hits equal to the number of models in the target unit.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c115" name="Reliable" hidden="false"><description>This weapon attacks using Quality 2+.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c116" name="Anti-Cover" hidden="false"><description>When attacking with this weapon, ignore the target's cover protection.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c117" name="Assault" hidden="false"><description>This ranged weapon can also be used when attacking in melee, instead of a melee weapon.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c118" name="Surge" hidden="false"><description>Unmodified rolls of 6 to hit with this weapon generate one additional hit. Only the original hit is treated as a roll of 6 for other special rules.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c119" name="Smash" hidden="false"><description>When attacking units beyond half of this weapon's range, the target must re-roll unmodified Defense results of 6.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c11a" name="Takedown" hidden="false"><description>When attacking with this weapon, the attacker may choose an individual model within the target unit to resolve the attack against, treating that model as a separate target for that attack.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c11b" name="Spell Amplifier" hidden="false"><description>This weapon improves the model's ability to cast spells, granting +1 to its spell casting rolls.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c11c" name="Thrust" hidden="false"><description>When charging, attacks with this weapon gain +1 to hit and AP(+1) in melee.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c11d" name="Deadly(X)" hidden="false"><description>An unsaved hit deals X wounds to a single model. Excess wounds do not carry over to other models.</description></rule><rule id="b174-c09d-3660-c11e" name="Unstoppable" hidden="false"><description>This weapon ignores Regeneration and all negative modifiers that do not come from the attacking model's own special rules.</description></rule><rule id="oprv36-rule-258" name="Evasive" hidden="false"><description>Enemies get -1 to hit rolls when attacking units where most models have this rule.</description></rule><rule id="oprv36-rule-259" name="Melee Shrouding" hidden="false"><description>When a unit where most models have this rule is targeted by an enemy unit for charging, that enemy unit gets -2" range to a minimum of 6".</description></rule><rule id="oprv36-rule-25a" name="Mend" hidden="false"><description>Once per activation, before attacking, pick one friendly model within 3" with Tough and remove D3 wounds from it.</description></rule><rule id="oprv36-rule-25b" name="Rapid Rush" hidden="false"><description>This model moves +6" when using Rush actions.</description></rule><rule id="oprv36-rule-25c" name="Re-Deployment" hidden="false"><description>After all other units are deployed (excluding set-aside units), remove up to two friendly units and deploy them again. Players alternate placing Re-Deployment units, starting with the player who activates next.</description></rule><rule id="oprv36-rule-25d" name="Steadfast" hidden="false"><description>If a unit where most models have this rule is Shaken at the beginning of the round, roll one die. On a 4+, it stops being Shaken.</description></rule><rule id="oprv36-rule-25e" name="Unstoppable Mark" hidden="false"><description>Once per activation, before attacking, pick one enemy unit within 18" in line of sight. Friendly units get Unstoppable on their weapons against that unit once (the next time the effect would apply).</description></rule><rule id="oprv36-rule-25f" name="Versatile Reach" hidden="false"><description>When this unit is activated, choose one effect: until the end of its activation, models with this rule in this unit either get +4" range when shooting or move +2" when charging.</description></rule><rule id="oprv36-rule-260" name="Bane in Melee Aura" hidden="false"><description>This model and its unit get Bane on their weapons in melee.</description></rule><rule id="oprv36-rule-261" name="Bane when Shooting Aura" hidden="false"><description>This model and its unit get Bane on their weapons when shooting.</description></rule><rule id="oprv36-rule-262" name="Bravery Aura" hidden="false"><description>This model and its unit get +1 to Morale test rolls.</description></rule><rule id="oprv36-rule-263" name="Melee Shrouding Aura" hidden="false"><description>This model and its unit get Melee Shrouding.</description></rule><rule id="oprv36-rule-264" name="Rapid Rush Aura" hidden="false"><description>This model and its unit get Rapid Rush.</description></rule><rule id="oprv36-rule-265" name="Regeneration Aura" hidden="false"><description>This model and its unit get Regeneration.</description></rule><rule id="oprv36-rule-266" name="Versatile Reach Aura" hidden="false"><description>This model and its unit get Versatile Reach.</description></rule><rule id="opr36-rules-1000000" name="Indirect" hidden="false"><description>May shoot at enemies outside line of sight when using a Hold action.</description></rule><rule id="opr36-rules-1000001" name="Limited" hidden="false"><description>This weapon can only be used once per game.</description></rule><rule id="opr36-rules-1000002" name="Rending" hidden="false"><description>Targets get -1 to Regeneration rolls, and unmodified hit rolls of 6 are resolved with AP(4).</description></rule><rule id="opr36-rules-1000003" name="Shred" hidden="false"><description>When targets roll unmodified results of 1 to block hits from this weapon, they suffer one additional wound.</description></rule><rule id="opr36-spell-1500000" name="Protective Dome (1)" hidden="false"><description>Pick one friendly unit within 12 inches, which gets Evasive once (the next time the effect would apply).</description></rule><rule id="opr36-spell-1500001" name="Psychic Terror (1)" hidden="false"><description>Pick one enemy unit within 6 inches, which takes 3 hits with Bane.</description></rule><rule id="opr36-spell-1500002" name="Advanced Sight (2)" hidden="false"><description>Pick up to two enemy units within 18 inches and line of sight. Friendly units get Unstoppable on their weapons when shooting those units once (the next time the effect would apply).</description></rule><rule id="opr36-spell-1500003" name="Lightning Fog (2)" hidden="false"><description>Pick up to two enemy units within 9 inches, which take 4 hits each.</description></rule><rule id="opr36-spell-1500004" name="Blessed Ammo (3)" hidden="false"><description>Pick up to three friendly units within 18 inches, which get Shred on their weapons when shooting once (the next time the effect would apply).</description></rule><rule id="opr36-spell-1500005" name="Cerebral Trauma (3)" hidden="false"><description>Pick one enemy unit within 24 inches and line of sight, which takes 6 hits with AP(1) and Smash.</description></rule><rule id="rl36-9ef457bfaf11" name="Self-Repair" hidden="false">
      <description>When a unit where most models have this rule takes wounds, roll one die for each. On a 6+ it is ignored.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-f5c4bf05b0d9" name="Ambushing Piercing Shot" hidden="false">
      <description>Counts as having Ambush, and its weapons get AP(+1) when shooting on the round in which it deploys via this rule.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-f9802ac20963" name="Casting Buff" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per activation, before attacking, pick one friendly model within 12" with Caster, which gets +1 to casting rolls once (next time the effect would apply).</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-16b8f02284e6" name="Enhanced Protected" hidden="false">
      <description>If most models in this unit have Protected, they ignore wounds on rolls of 5-6 from Protected (instead of only on 6+).</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-e92f5769c7a5" name="Enhanced Self-Repair" hidden="false">
      <description>If most models in this unit have Self-Repair, they ignore wounds on rolls of 5-6 from Self-Repair (instead of only on 6+).</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-d529c8bb39f8" name="Enhanced Self-Repair Buff" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per activation, before attacking, pick one friendly unit within 12", which gets Enhanced Self-Repair once (next time the effect would apply).</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-cb200f2d4cf3" name="Imprecise" hidden="false">
      <description>Gets -1 to hit when attacking.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-2a2d6244d1b5" name="Indirect Mark" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per activation, before attacking, pick one enemy unit within 18" in line of sight, which friendly units gets Indirect on their weapons against once (next time the effect would apply).</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-483ef483642e" name="Infiltrate" hidden="false">
      <description>Counts as having Ambush, but may be deployed anywhere over 3" away from enemy unit.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-090062551e31" name="No Retreat" hidden="false">
      <description>When a unit where most models have this rule fails a Morale Test that causes it to be Shaken or Routed, the test counts as passed instead. Then, roll as many dice as the number of wounds it would take to fully destroy it, and for each result of 1-3 the unit takes one wound, which cannot be ignored.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-bceadeec5c00" name="Piercing Charge" hidden="false">
      <description>This model gets AP(+1) on its weapons when charging.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-758e54fe2903" name="Protected" hidden="false">
      <description>When a unit where most models have this rule takes wounds, roll one die for each. On a 6+ it is ignored.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-495620287019" name="Protection Feat" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per game, when this unit takes wounds and most of its models have this rule, you may use this rule and roll one die per wound, and on a 5+ it is ignored.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-0ba8e40363a2" name="Rapid Advance" hidden="false">
      <description>This model moves +4" when using Advance actions.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-f19224e322ed" name="Ravage" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per round, when it is this model's turn to strike in melee, roll X dice before attacking, unless this unit is Fatigued. For each 6+ the target takes one wound.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-2a9240a5f23f" name="Reanimation" hidden="false">
      <description>When a unit where all models have this rule is activated, roll as many dice as the max. number of models/wounds it could restore. For each 5+ you may restore one model/wound. New models may only be restored if they can be placed in coherency with non-restored models.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-0f4202adb40f" name="Repel Ambushers" hidden="false">
      <description>Enemy units using Ambush must be set up over 12" away from this model's unit.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-441da07c76f7" name="Shatter" hidden="false">
      <description>For each unmodified result of 6 to hit, those hits get AP(+3).</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-1c09f9c5aaea" name="Spawn" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per game, when this model is activated, you may place a new unit of X fully within 6" of it. Units placed via Spawn cannot seize or contest objectives on the round they are placed.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-2171364187e2" name="Stealth Buff" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per activation, before attacking, pick one friendly unit within 12", which gets Stealth once (next time the effect would apply).</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-a8e21da73bba" name="Swift" hidden="false">
      <description>This model may ignore the Slow rule.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-3978b014ad7f" name="Swift Buff" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per activation, before attacking, pick one friendly unit within 12", which gets Swift once (next time the effect would apply).</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-4da0eb86b73d" name="Unique Hero" hidden="false">
      <description>Counts as having Hero, and this model may only be taken once per army.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-d237c116a8c7" name="Ambush Aura" hidden="false">
      <description>This model and its unit get Ambush.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-67073d81cd29" name="No Retreat Aura" hidden="false">
      <description>This model and its unit get No Retreat.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-44ad4e3c982c" name="Piercing Charge Aura" hidden="false">
      <description>This model and its unit get Piercing Charge.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-4d48fa9be073" name="Protection Feat Aura" hidden="false">
      <description>This model and its unit get Protection Feat.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-e120f56e0521" name="Reanimation Aura" hidden="false">
      <description>This model and its unit get Reanimation.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-7129e4757f3b" name="Relentless Aura" hidden="false">
      <description>This model and its unit get Relentless.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-6c0a30aef180" name="Stealth Aura" hidden="false">
      <description>This model and its unit get Stealth.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-38c64799d510" name="Unstoppable when Shooting Aura" hidden="false">
      <description>This model and its unit get Unstoppable on its weapons when shooting.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-4e37395d9f1c" name="Triangulation Bots (1)" hidden="false">
      <description>Pick one enemy unit within 18" in line of sight, which friendly units gets Indirect on their weapons against once (next time the effect would apply).</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-d3598b1071f6" name="Gauss Bots (1)" hidden="false">
      <description>Pick one enemy unit within 6", which takes 3 hits with AP(1) and Shatter. Roll as many dice as hits to see if "on rolls of 6" effects trigger.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-52fb19e75031" name="Inspiring Bots (2)" hidden="false">
      <description>Pick up to two friendly units within 12", which get Rapid Advance once (next time the effect would apply).</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-68418f69a195" name="Flame Bots (2)" hidden="false">
      <description>Pick up to two enemy units within 9", which take 4 hits each.</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-5c2dd80e9b81" name="Mending Bots (3)" hidden="false">
      <description>Pick up to three friendly units within 18", which get Enhanced Self-Repair once (next time the effect would apply).</description>
    </rule><rule id="rl36-103277c9cb1a" name="Piercing Bots (3)" hidden="false">
      <description>Pick one enemy unit within 18" in line of sight, which takes 6 hits with AP(2).</description>
    </rule><rule id="cust-36-0000001" name="Guardian" hidden="false"><description>When units where most models have this rule take hits, those hits count as having AP(-1), to a minimum of AP(0).</description></rule><rule id="cust-36-0000002" name="Disintegrate" hidden="false"><description>Ignores Regeneration, and when attacking units where most models have Tough(3) or higher, this weapon gets AP(+2).</description></rule><rule id="cust-36-0000003" name="Dodge" hidden="false"><description>If most models in this unit have this rule, as long as they aren't Fatigued, enemy units get -1 to hit rolls in melee against them.</description></rule><rule id="cust-36-0000004" name="Enhanced Guardian" hidden="false"><description>If most models in this unit have Guardian, hits they take count as having AP(-2) from Guardian (instead of only AP(-1)).</description></rule><rule id="cust-36-0000005" name="Enhanced Fortified" hidden="false"><description>If most models in this unit have Fortified, hits they take count as having AP(-2) from Fortified.</description></rule><rule id="cust-36-0000006" name="Fortified" hidden="false"><description>When units where most models have this rule take hits, those hits count as having AP(-1), to a minimum of AP(0).</description></rule><rule id="cust-36-0000007" name="Hit &amp; Run" hidden="false"><description>Once per round, this model may move by up to 3 inches after shooting or being in melee.</description></rule><rule id="cust-36-0000008" name="Hit &amp; Run Shooter" hidden="false"><description>Once per round, this model may move by up to 3 inches after shooting.</description></rule><rule id="cust-36-0000009" name="Ranged Shrouding" hidden="false"><description>When a unit where most models have this rule is targeted for shooting, enemy unit gets -4 inches range, minimum 6 inches.</description></rule><rule id="cust-36-0000010" name="Shred Mark" hidden="false"><description>Once per activation, before attacking, pick one enemy unit within 18 inches in line of sight; friendly units get Shred against it once.</description></rule><rule id="cust-36-0000011" name="Unpredictable Fighter" hidden="false"><description>When in melee, roll a die: on 1-3 this model gets AP(+1), on 4-6 gets +1 to hit rolls.</description></rule><rule id="cust-36-0000012" name="Dash" hidden="false"><description>Once per round, at the end of this unit's activation, move models with this rule up to D3+1 inches.</description></rule><rule id="cust-36-0000013" name="Piercing Target(X)" hidden="false"><description>Once per game, mark X enemy units within 18 inches and line of sight; friendly units get AP(+1) when attacking them.</description></rule><rule id="cust-36-0000014" name="Enhanced Guardian Aura" hidden="false"><description>This model and its unit get Enhanced Guardian.</description></rule><rule id="cust-36-0000015" name="Hit &amp; Run Shooter Aura" hidden="false"><description>This model and its unit get Hit &amp; Run Shooter.</description></rule><rule id="cust-36-0000016" name="Unstoppable in Melee Aura" hidden="false"><description>This model and its unit get Unstoppable on weapons in melee.</description></rule><rule id="cust-36-0000017" name="Shred when Shooting Aura" hidden="false"><description>This model and its unit get Shred on weapons when shooting.</description></rule><rule id="cust-36-0000018" name="Steadfast Aura" hidden="false"><description>This model and its unit get Steadfast.</description></rule><rule id="cust-36-0000019" name="Dash Aura" hidden="false"><description>This model and its unit get Dash.</description></rule><rule id="cust-36-0000020" name="Ranged Shrouding Aura" hidden="false"><description>This model and its unit get Ranged Shrouding.</description></rule><rule id="cust-36-0000021" name="Unstoppable in Melee" hidden="false"><description>This model's melee weapons get Unstoppable.</description></rule><rule id="cust-36-0000022" name="Shred when Shooting" hidden="false"><description>This model's shooting weapons get Shr